  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "12. Fight Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "12.03",
    "summary": "A unit may make a pile-in move of up to 3\" in the [Fight Phase (12.00)](vsdata:core-rule/fight-phase), following [Moving (03.00)](vsdata:core-rule/moving). Units are chosen for it in the [Pile In Step (12.02)](vsdata:core-rule/pile-in-step).\n\nIt is eligible if at least one of these is true:\n\n- it is engaged ([Engagement (03.04)](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range));\n- it charged this turn ([Charge Move (11.04)](vsdata:core-rule/charge-move));\n- it was chosen for an overrun fight in this phase ([Overrun Fight (12.06)](vsdata:core-rule/overrun-fight)).\n\nBefore moving, pick its pile-in targets:\n\n- an engaged unit takes all enemy units engaged with it;\n- any other unit takes at least 1 enemy unit within 5\" of it.\n\nWhile moving:\n\n- a model in base contact with an enemy model cannot move;\n- each model that moves must end closer to its nearest pile-in target, ending engaged with it where it can.\n\nAfter moving:\n\n- the unit ends engaged;\n- each model that began the move engaged with any enemy unit stays engaged with that unit.",
